{
  "info": {
    "name": "Wagering (Pegasus)",
    "description": "Control plane for the wagering service, the host Pegasus runs on (kernel/api). One host; routes are generic over the application: {{app}} = pegasus.\n\nGetting started:\n1. Run SESSION and the wagering binary (JWK_URL = SESSION's JWKS, JWT_ISSUER = SESSION's issuer, SETTINGS_URL = file:///some/dir or s3://bucket/prefix).\n2. Set sessionUrl, username/password (a user with the pegasus role) and adminUsername/adminPassword (a user with the admin role).\n3. Send both requests in \"Auth (SESSION)\". They store token and adminToken; requests use token unless marked admin. SESSION access tokens are short lived: log in again on a 401.\n\nFirst run, in order:\n1. Admin settings: Save betfair (Pegasus cannot start without it), Save triples (or set enabled false), Save tpd.\n2. System (admin): Restart, then Status shows each feed and any start error.\n3. Process settings: Save settings. Process lifecycle: Add, Start.\n\nStatus codes: 400 invalid input or settings (the body says why), 401 missing/bad token, 403 not admin or another user's process, 404 unknown app/document/process, 409 runtime state conflict, or saved but not reloaded.\n\nVariables:\n- baseUrl: http://localhost:<WAGERING_PORT> (through ADMIN: http://localhost:3001/wagering-api)\n- app: pegasus\n- processId: the process to act on\n- userId: a SESSION user id, used only where the userId query param is enabled, with the admin token",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminUsername",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "app",
      "value": "pegasus"
    },
    {
      "key": "processId",
      "value": "local-test-1"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "admin only: the user to act for"
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth (SESSION)",
      "description": "Logs in against SESSION and stores the access token in a collection variable.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (user)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', body.access_token);",
                  "console.log('roles', body.user && body.user.roles);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"username\": \"{{username}}\", \"password\": \"{{password}}\"}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sessionUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{sessionUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
