    {
      "name": "Process settings",
      "description": "A process is one settings document at settings/processes/<app>/<user_id>/<processId>.json. PUT is the whole document: it is decoded into the app's settings type (unknown fields refused) and Validate() runs before anything is written.\n\n- 204: saved. If the runtime has the process loaded it is rebuilt from the new document and left running if it was.\n- 400: invalid; the body is the reason, e.g. \"invalid settings: scope US/THOROUGHBRED betmatic delay must be at least 500ms\".\n- 409: saved, but the loaded process did not rebuild from it; the body says why.\n\nWorks while the runtime is stopped. Enable the userId query param (with the admin token) to act for another user.",
